ul.li:
Verify as_signature on each delegation record using the
signing key of the AS that issued that record (which may differ
across records);

delegation_chain claim: An explicit,
cryptographically signed audit trail of all delegation hops,
which identity-chaining does not define;

Dual-signature security: Both AS and
delegating agent sign each delegation record, preventing
unilateral forgery;

Evidence propagation: Root user consent
evidence (root_evidence_ref) is preserved across
the chain;

When the AS determines that a delegation requires user consent,
it returns an interaction_required response as defined
by JAG-IR, rather than a direct error;

The delegating agent launches the interaction_uri
provided by the AS, enabling the user to review and approve
the delegation details;

